<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42667" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sarsĭna</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sassĭna</span></b> ), ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An ancient town in Umbria</i>, <i>the
				birthplace of Plautus</i>, still called <i>Sarsina</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 9, 59, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8,
			463</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sarsĭnātis</span></b> , e (collat.
			form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sassĭnas</span></b> ,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4404</span></i>; 
				v.
				infra
			), adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Sarsina</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sassinate de silvā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 3, 58, 35</span></i>
			.—In a lusus verbb., <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Most. 3, 2, 83</span></i>.—In <i>plur.
			subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sarsĭnātes</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sass-</span></b> ),
			ĭum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Sarsina</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 14,
				19, § 114</span></i>.</div>
